during the proccess of making my battery pack for my 3kw gocart, I needed a spotwelder. after a bit of research i relised i could just make one myself from a car battery and a super duper simple circult with basic mosfets, it would be unreliable, as the timing would be based purely on my click speed, but it would get the job done. i didnt doument much of this build. but basically i made 2 copper probes, silliconed them to a stick, wired up the two probes to the pos and neg outputs of the mosfets, added a mechanical swithc that activated a side circuit, that then activated the main circuit, which shorted out the car battery trhough the mosfet for a few seconds. this was enough to weld two super thin nickel strips togetehr. unfortunately it was also enough to blow the 4 mosfets i used. i got the mosfets from a old ebike motor controller that was broken. i also printed this breadboard type thing, 3d printed thing with a bunch of small holes in it, its the only photo i have of the project.
